  "worked_solution": "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(8,8).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(8,8),$ we can substitute $x=8$ and $y=8$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {8}^{2} & =4p(8) \\\\ 64 & =32p \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(2)x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =8x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=2$ is positive.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
